kernel-wedge for the Trisquel udebs of this kernel
==================================================

Origin: Debian linux 7.0.13-1, debian/installer/kernel-wedge/ (Debian merged
kernel-wedge into its linux package and maintains it there). It is shipped
here so this kernel does not depend on the distro kernel-wedge package, which
in ecne is the 2.96ubuntu3 versiom needed by the base 6.8 kernel.

Used by debian/rules.d/5-udebs.mk (copy-modules, find-dups, find-unpackaged,
check) and debian/scripts/trisquel-gen-udeb-control.sh (gen-control), with
KW_CONFIG_DIR=$(DEBIAN)/d-i. Packages are selected by the Architecture: fields
of d-i/package-list; the kernel-image udeb content (vmlinuz, System.map,
modules.order, modules.builtin, dtbs) is added by 5-udebs.mk.

Trisquel changes, keep them when updating from Debian:
 - copy-modules: modules go to /lib/modules: Trixie's debian-installer, which
   builds the netinst, reads /lib/modules (Debian >= 7.0 udebs moved to
   /usr/lib/modules).
 - copy-modules: no postinst running depmod, as in the udebs built so far.
 - find-dups: skip udebs without modules (e.g. armhf ata-modules, libata is
   built-in)

--- a/copy-modules
+++ b/copy-modules
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@
 use lib dirname(__FILE__);
 use KernelWedge qw(read_package_lists for_each_package package_enabled);
 
-my $prefix = '/usr';
+my $prefix = '';
 my $kw_bin_dir = dirname(__FILE__);
 
 my $version = "${ARGV[0]}-${ARGV[1]}";
@@ -154,12 +154,6 @@
 		$cpio_pipe->print("$_\n") for keys %mods;
 		close($cpio_pipe);
 
-		open(my $postinst_fh, '>', "debian/$i-$version-di.postinst");
-		$postinst_fh->print(<<~EOF);
-		#!/bin/sh -e
-		depmod $installedname
-		EOF
-		close($postinst_fh);
 	}
 }
 close($deps_sort_pipe);
--- a/find-dups
+++ b/find-dups
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@
 		else
 			moddir=lib/modules/$kernel
 		fi
-		find $moddir -type f -printf "$dir %p\n"
+		[ ! -d $moddir ] || find $moddir -type f -printf "$dir %p\n"
 		cd ../..
 	done
 ) | sort -k2 | perl -ne '
